Advantages:
Demonstrates real Linux system calls.
Provides practical understanding of file descriptors.
Demonstrates directory traversal.
Provides basic file management functionality.
Uses modular C programming.
Can be extended with additional features.

Disadvantages:
The application is command-line based.
Directory deletion is limited to empty directories.
File permissions and ownership changes are not implemented.
The program is primarily designed for Linux systems.
The interface does not provide graphical file management.
